{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02444",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.59,
      "end_seconds": 3.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting, come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.79,
      "end_seconds": 9.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Hi doctor, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.3,
      "end_seconds": 13.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.0,
      "end_seconds": 25.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.57,
      "text": "Uh, you know, it's itchy spots all over, mostly. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.18,
      "end_seconds": 28.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Alright, since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.69,
      "end_seconds": 38.29,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "Well, it's been going on for two weeks. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.19,
      "end_seconds": 41.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.55,
      "end_seconds": 60.71,
      "duration_seconds": 18.16,
      "text": "Severe, I'd say. As for mild temperature, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. Uh, with mild temperature, it feels severe to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.71,
      "end_seconds": 64.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Right, have you been feeling achy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.42,
      "end_seconds": 66.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Yes, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.59,
      "end_seconds": 74.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any stiff neck, breathlessness, pregnancy or being immunosuppressed?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.22,
      "end_seconds": 78.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Erm, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.49,
      "end_seconds": 81.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.39,
      "end_seconds": 87.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "No, um, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.14,
      "end_seconds": 92.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.67,
      "end_seconds": 95.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.15,
      "end_seconds": 99.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.2,
      "end_seconds": 116.5,
      "duration_seconds": 15.3,
      "text": "It's spironolactone, 25 milligrams, once a day for my heart. It's pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast for my acidity. Carvedilol I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.56,
      "end_seconds": 126.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.09,
      "end_seconds": 131.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Just a varicose vein procedure, last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.86,
      "end_seconds": 133.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.15,
      "end_seconds": 138.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.04,
      "end_seconds": 147.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.24,
      "end_seconds": 152.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.98,
      "end_seconds": 155.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.93,
      "end_seconds": 165.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.38,
      "end_seconds": 181.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Right, do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.98,
      "end_seconds": 201.89,
      "duration_seconds": 18.91,
      "text": "I've had heart failure for two years now. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, you know, to be honest. I have acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.48,
      "end_seconds": 217.09,
      "duration_seconds": 10.61,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Right, so heart failure is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Right, I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.16,
      "end_seconds": 228.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.9,
      "end_seconds": 254.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 98 percent, heart rate 85. And BP is 114 over 81, temperature is 36.4 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.93,
      "end_seconds": 261.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.28,
      "end_seconds": 263.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.25,
      "end_seconds": 266.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "So, look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.97,
      "end_seconds": 290.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "There are crops of blisters and scabs in different stages on the trunk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.6,
      "end_seconds": 303.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.36,
      "text": "So, all finished, thank you. Let me tell you where I've got to. This is probably chickenpox. Shingles is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.66,
      "end_seconds": 310.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Mm, um, is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.21,
      "end_seconds": 317.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like chickenpox."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.28,
      "end_seconds": 352.18,
      "duration_seconds": 23.9,
      "text": "The treatment will be aciclovir, 800 milligrams, five times a day, seven days. It's for adult chickenpox. Stay at home until all the spots have crusted and stay away from pregnant women. If you become breathless or have chest pain, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.56,
      "end_seconds": 357.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.86,
      "end_seconds": 366.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "Book a review if you become breathless. Let me check I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.12,
      "end_seconds": 384.66,
      "duration_seconds": 12.54,
      "text": "So, I take the aciclovir, 800 milligrams, five times a day and come back if you become breathless. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.45,
      "end_seconds": 393.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. So, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.15,
      "end_seconds": 397.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.26,
      "end_seconds": 400.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}